      "proposed_content": "A finite check can calibrate the smooth zero count and its half-cycle offset while leaving microscopic fluctuations unexplained. In the inverse xp construction, inserting fluctuation curvature into a geometric boundary can destroy monotonicity and produce multivalued branches, whereas the proposed operator constraint stores the differentiated fluctuation count in the phase of a boundary-state Mellin amplitude.",
