    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ef812117f309e0e9a2f19960c9e8262fe6ad1879cc38b63f22437c98d14e2045",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In the cokernel model, multiplication by an L-function forces compactly supported Mellin distributions onto its zeros, and delta derivatives up to the zero-order and Sobolev bounds become generalized eigenvectors; nontrivial Jordan depth thus records multiplicity. In the non-Hermitian proposal, off-critical zeros are instead assigned coalescing, self-orthogonal exceptional-point states. Jordan structure therefore has model-dependent semantics and cannot by itself diagnose off-criticality.",
